    // Bennus Project
    bennusTitle: 'Bennus: Full-Stack Meal Delivery E-commerce',
    bennusDesc: 'Production e-commerce platform for meal delivery with custom meal builder and comprehensive admin panel.',
    bennusDetailDesc: 'Bennus is a production-grade full-stack e-commerce platform built for a real meal delivery business. The platform implements a sophisticated dual shopping experience: customers can purchase pre-configured meal packages or leverage the custom meal builder to compose personalized meals from available components. Architected entirely with Next.js 16 for both frontend and backend, the system leverages MySQL with Prisma ORM for reliable data persistence and complex queries. The checkout flow integrates WhatsApp for order finalization, providing a pragmatic alternative to traditional payment gateways while maintaining a frictionless user experience. The admin dashboard provides complete business control: product management, real-time inventory tracking, dynamic pricing, category organization, and order analytics. The platform is optimized for performance, fully responsive, and designed with scalability in mind from the ground up.',
    bennusFeatures: ['Dual Shopping Model (Pre-configured & Custom Meals)', 'Advanced Meal Builder with Real-time Pricing', 'Persistent Shopping Cart with State Management', 'WhatsApp Order Integration', 'Full-Featured Admin Dashboard', 'Inventory Management with Stock Alerts', 'Dynamic Pricing Engine', 'Category & Product Organization', 'Order Tracking & Analytics', 'Image Management & Optimization', 'Role-Based Access Control', 'Server-Side Rendering', 'Database Query Optimization', 'Mobile-First Responsive Design'],
    bennusChallenges: 'Building a production e-commerce system with Next.js as the full-stack framework required careful architectural decisions. Key technical challenges included designing a flexible meal builder that handles complex product combinations with accurate real-time pricing calculations, implementing robust inventory management to prevent overselling while maintaining performance, architecting a WhatsApp integration that preserves order context and product details reliably, building an admin panel with intuitive workflows for non-technical users, optimizing database queries for fast product filtering and search across large datasets, ensuring data consistency between shopping cart state and inventory systems, and managing image uploads with proper optimization. Additionally, implementing secure server actions for data mutations, handling concurrent requests efficiently, and maintaining excellent performance metrics required production-level engineering practices.',
    bennusLearnings: 'This project reinforced production-level full-stack development practices with Next.js. I deepened my expertise in server components, server actions, and API route architecture. Working with Prisma and MySQL at scale taught me advanced patterns for query optimization, transaction management, and data consistency. The meal builder feature required sophisticated state management and real-time calculations, enhancing my ability to handle complex business logic. Developing the admin panel reinforced the importance of thoughtful UX for business tools and comprehensive CRUD operations. The WhatsApp integration demonstrated pragmatic solutions for order processing without traditional payment infrastructure. Most importantly, this project validated my ability to deliver production systems that solve real business problems, manage technical complexity, and scale with business growth.',

